c013c97942 Add a harness mode that pictures the printer connect flow

--printer-connect-capture <dir> connects a Klipper printer through the
real printer panel with the live model (OPENAI_API_KEY), against print
hosts on loopback ports that fail after a hold, never answer, or answer.
It writes a PNG of the panel at each state of the connect card:
the card, Connecting…, a question asked while waiting, failed,
cancelled, connected, and Home afterwards.

The pictures come from WKWebView's own snapshot
(harness_appearance.mm), because a harness started from a shell has no
Screen Recording permission on macOS: screencapture and the harness's
screen blit get nothing there. The mode is macOS-only for that reason.

Ran once end to end: all seven pictures written, no failed checks.

